You've probably set up an alias in your .cshrc or .bashrc files.

One alias I came across for su was something like 
alias su=/sbin/su $*
instaed of 
alias su=/sbin/su "$@"

Where the latter ensures that anything in quotes remains as one
argument, and the former breaks all quoted objects up into their bits
separated by spaces.

