If there's nothing in the error log (uerf or DECevent or EVM, whatever 
you happen to be using -- can't remember what's used on your OS 
version), then I would suspect strongly a power-related problem, 
including any connectors and switches that might tell the system to shut 
down.  I've lost track of how many problems such as the one you're 
facing were the result of loose/flaky mating connectors, airflow sensors 
and the cables that run to them, marginal AC cords, even had a problem 
one where the loose wire was in the actual power box up in the bus bar.

I'd also try reseating everything you can get your hands on, beginning 
with all CPU and memory cards and all the cards in the IO slots.

QH



