I've done both (http://www.usit.uio.no/it/unix/du/versions.txt).
You need to go v4.0F -> v5.0A -> v5.1A

In my experience it's far better to do a reinstallation 
(http://www.usit.uio.no/it/unix/du/reinstallere-v51A.txt and files
mentioned below in that page. It's in Norwegian, but all commands
should tell you what to do :)

All this is documented for my site, you may have other requirements.
But it's throughly tested.

As long as you have /, swap, /usr and /var on the system disk(s) and
all data elsewhere *) there is no problem to mount them after 
reinstallation just by making the correct directories in /etc/fdmns 
with underlying links to the devices and fix (copy back) the needed 
lines in fstab.

The reinstallation made me also repartition som disks because /
needed to expand.
*) Data might live on the system disk - but then you need to 
conserve this data partitions and modify partitions a (/), 
b (swap1) and usr(+var)-partition(s) only (g or d).

Hope this is usefull to you!

Regards,
