The Tru64 UNIX v4.0f AdvFS file systems will continue to work on v5.1a.  
There should be no problem.

While AdvFS on Tru64 UNIX v5.* uses some new on-disk format information, 
AdvFS still works with prior AdvFS domains.

The 2 areas where AdvFS has improved when a domain is created on a v5.* 
system is that Directories have a btree structure for faster lookup, 
create, delete of huge directories (and I do mean huge).

The 2nd important change was the way the AdvFS BMT metadata file was 
managed.  On domains created prior to Tru64 UNIX v5.*, it was possible 
to run out of extent map entries for the BMT.  On v5.* systems, this is 
no longer possible.

A few other misc changes were made, like allowing 64K subdirectories per 
directory instead of 32K, etc...

The conversion method is to do a backup and restore, or if the existing 
domains are working just the way you like them, then leave them alone.  
AdvFS will use them as they are.

                                        Bob Harris


