OK That just means you are using a version of Tru64 older than V5 and so
you are using the old device naming.
You can either do as you have done and user /dev/rrz* or you can work
in a slightly different fashion.
You know which scsi bus you device is connected to, you know the scsi
target id and you know the lun.
Start scu without pointing it at a file at all.
Then inside scu, type
set nexus bus B target T lun L
Where BT and L are bus target and Lun respectively.
The in program help of scu is quite good, read the help text for format
and it should give details.
HTH
Adam






