> They are nice disks, so I have to low-level format them somehow, is
> there a utility under one of those two operating systems to do that?

You need to set the SCSI drive's mode page to 512 byte sectors *before*
you format, and you need to do this consistently so that the format will
work.

On an Ultrix box you can do this with rzdisk -c; the mode pages that you'll
have to tweak will include Page 3 (device format parameters) and Page 4
(rigid disk drive geometry parameters).

Tim.


