Roman Prokhorov <roma@stalker.gamma.ru> writes:

> I have a problem: Under Tru64 the fork() called from a thread freezes. 
> This doesn't happen on the other Unixes I tried. See my code below, did 
> I do anything wrong? 

Yes. 

Your question has been answered many times in comp.programming.threads.
Search groups.google.com for "thread fork async" ... 

Here is one answer by Kaz Kylheku 
Message-ID: <slrn8urucn.gqp.kaz@ashi.FootPrints.net>

    Mind you, according to POSIX, if a threaded process forks a
    child, that child can execute only async safe functions. It
    can use exec() to load a new process image. Since fprintf()
    is not async safe, calling it results in undefined behavior.

Cheers,
-- 
