> OK, what mutexes are locked by fgets? Are they documented anywhere?

It is unlikely that fgets needs other mutexes (it may need malloc
mutex at times). It is also unlikely that these mutexes are
documented anywhere.

Even if they were, you are missing the point:

    > How to make it to create all the files 
    > _while_ it's waiting for the input? 

which is that you *can't* reliably fork() multithreaded programs,
unless you wrote *all* the code [including libc]. Since you
did not write libc [and I hope you don't plan on it ;-], you just
can't fork().

Accept this fact, and move on to one of the other solutions.

Cheers,
