On Tue, 13 Aug 2002 19:13:51 +0200, TTT wrote:

> Any caveats/tips/tricks/warnings/words of wisdom will be greatly 
> appreciated.

Here's how we're going about a similar exercise (no memory upgrade in
our case):

Use a physically (ie the disks are all StorageWorks in our case) and
binary (all Alpha servers in our case) compatible test system onto which
you install the 5.1A system and any software you install locally.

Once you're satisfied that everything works correctly, make sure to
adjust hostname and IP address configurations to be correct for the
production system(s).  Repeat as necessary, and as replacement disks are
available.

Schedule downtime on your production systems for the upgrade, and when
the time comes, simply swap the disks.  Come up in single-user mode and
check the system for basic sanity.  You'll probably need to make some
adjustments before everything is just right, but you should have a
mostly sane installation, and you have a quick way to backout, should
the need to do so arise.

I hope that helps...

