> rob    pts/2        ::ffff:192.168.2 Wed Aug 14 11:28 - 11:31  (00:03)

This is an IPv4-mapped IPv6 address (we now store all addresses in the
kernel as IPv6 addresses) that simply isn't getting printed right by one
of the libc routines.  The problem has since been fixed in v5.1a, I'm not
sure if there are plans to backport it since it's only a cosmetic thing that
can happen when we can't resolve an IP address to a name.

-Brian Haley, HP Tru64 Unix Networking



