Easy fix in such situations: Have a *BSD or Linux PC with SCSI and a
recent CDROM/DVD drive near you. In most cases, the recent drives have
better error recovery, and may copy the Tru64 install CD on a spare
700MB-1GB old SCSI clunker. That is how I installed hobbyist VMS, since
the old SCSI CDROM drive did not read the CDs correctly.

Less trouble, and it might even be faster!
