On 2 Aug 2002 05:15:23 -0700, Jack Frillman wrote:

> Did you need to do anything special to get it to compile?

No.  My transcript says I did the following (this is rather condensed,
but all the steps are there):

  sh Configure
  make
  make test
  make install
  make clean
  cd /usr/include
  /local/bin/perl-5.004/h2ph * sys/* mach/* mach/machine/*
  chmod -R a+rX,og-w /local/lib/perl-5.004

(Hrmmm...  I realize that on the system I copied that transcript from,
the Perl version is even older than I'd thought, but the idea is the
same.  I've never had any trouble installing Perl on any system, and I
do have 5.005 on a few...)

